# basePath Chapter1
:: FirstContractOpenCh1
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene
@once

{@PAL}      Welcome to the Frontier Robotics employee orientation! 
{@Player}   Wait... I own this ship. I'm not an employee!
{@PAL}      When you signed up to automate your ship’s fabrication system with Frontier Robotics you technically became an employee.


{@PAL}      Your first “contract” is your orientation. 
$call   HighlightElement(overarching:costs-section, false, 25, true)
{@PAL}      This shows how long we expect the contract to take you.
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
$call   HighlightElement(overarching:profit-section, false, 25, true)
{@PAL}      ...and this is the full payment for a successful delivery.
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
{@Player}   I miss my old team. I've never done any of this myself. 
{@PAL}      I'm your Personal Automation Liaison (P.A.L.) and I'm WAY more useful than human assistants.
 {@Player} 	...hmmmm... 
 {@PAL}      You can start with the Research Lab or Chip Design. 


$call   HighlightElement(overarching:select-contract-btn)
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Basic Conductor")
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Basic Insulator")
$call   LockWikiPage("Conductor") // only Basic Conductor is available in first chapter 
$call   LockWikiPage("Insulator") // only Basic Insulator is available in first chapter 

:: FirstContractAcceptCh1
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene 
@once
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()




:: BeforeSupplyChainCh1
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene
@once
{@Player}    I think I'm ready to build the chips now, right? 
{@PAL}       Not quite. You’ll need materials first. Nothing our new Supply Console system can’t handle.
{@Player}	I'm going to give Quinn a call to let her know she'll be working with me. 
//phone dial character
{@Quinn}    Oh, hi Locke! I was expecting to see Dorian. 
{@Player}   Yeah, Dorian's not on the ship anyore. It's a long story but I'm planning the routes now. 
{@Quinn}    Okay, Cap'. I’ve got you.
{@Quinn}    You decide where you want to get your materials. I’ll handle the haulers.
{@Player} Sounds easy enough. Talk to you later.


